{"id": "3022", "revid": "2288211", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=3022", "title": "Bay City (Michigan)", "text": "Bay City is a city in Central Michigan. A former lumbering/mill town that was incorporated in 1865, it was at one time the home of the celebrity Madonna, which is commemorated in a mural downtown.\nGet in.\nBy car.\nBay City is accessible from I-75 / US-23 and US-10 highways.\nBy bus.\nBay City is served by Greyhound Bus Lines through Indian Trails.\nDo.\nThe Riverwalk located along the Saginaw river. Features artwork, gardens, softball fields and a children's playground.\nDrink.\nVisit Bay City's Midland Street for a wide variety of pubs, bars and clubs set in with local shops and restaurants. The area is part of the historic down town of West Bay City."}
{"id": "3023", "revid": "2441334", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=3023", "title": "Bay City (Texas)", "text": "Bay City is a small city in the Gulf Coast region of Texas. It's on SH-35, about two hours from Houston, at the Colorado River.\nGet in.\nAccess exclusively by private car. From Houston, locate SH-35 (it crosses IH-45 just south of down town, inside the loop), and go south for about two hours.\nGet around.\nCar, foot, bike, or taxi"}
