{"id": "3144", "revid": "2441334", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=3144", "title": "Bedford (Indiana)", "text": "Bedford is a town in Southern Indiana, 20 mi south of Bloomington. It is the county seat of Lawrence County. \nGet in.\nTraffic entering Bedford from Bloomington and farther north from Indianapolis can use IN 37 southbound, while areas to the south near Paoli and Interstate 64 will use IN 37 northbound. From the east, US 50 westbound brings traffic from Seymour and Interstate 65. Areas to the west like Vincennes will follow US 50 eastbound. From the southeast, IN 60 (at Mitchell) brings traffic from Salem and Louisville.\nEat.\nIn addition to local fare, Bedford has several chain restaurants such as Golden Corral (\"1521 James Ave\"), Domino's (\"1605 M St.\"), Pizza Hut (\"2111 West 16th St.\", and Little Caesars (\"2605 16th St\").\nConnect.\nThe zip code is 47421.\nBy phone.\nMost telephone numbers in Bedford consist of +1 812 plus a seven-digit number, while others use +1 930. A local or in-state telephone call requires all 10 digits of the local number be dialed (omitting just the leading +1 from a local landline call).\nSignage on many established businesses may still display the original seven-digit numbers; dial 812 before these if no area code is indicated."}
{"id": "3145", "revid": "2441334", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=3145", "title": "Bedford (Massachusetts)", "text": "Bedford is a town in Massachusetts with a population of 14,000 (2020).\nCarlisle is a town with a population of 5,000 (2020). A low population density gives the town a rural feel, and it's known for outdoor activities including hiking and biking.\nGet in.\nBy car.\nDriving is the easiest way to get to Bedford and Carlisle. If coming from the Boston area, take MA-2 and Lowell Rd, or from I-95, and take the exit for MA-225 west.\nBy bus.\nThe MBTA operates the 62 bus to Bedford Monday through Saturday, service every 50-75 minutes.\nBy bicycle.\nBedford and Carlisle are popular destinations for cyclists. Many enter on Concord Rd or Bedford Rd. The wildly popular Minuteman Bikeway begins in Cambridge and terminates near Bedford Center. Several options like the Bruce Freeman Rail Trail branch out from there.\nGet around.\nGiven the infrequent nature of the 62 bus, driving and biking are the easiest ways to get around.\nDo.\nTown owned conservation lands can be found throughout Carlisle and all areas have hiking trails.\nGo next.\nConcord is the town directly to the south of Carlisle, known for its history in the American Revolution and for its famous authors. Lowell is a 20 minute drive north of Carlisle Center."}
{"id": "3146", "revid": "2441334", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=3146", "title": "Bedford (New Hampshire)", "text": "Bedford is a city of 23,000 people (2020) in New Hampshire. It is a suburb of Manchester, New Hampshire's largest city.\nGet in.\nBy car.\nTwo major highways run through Bedford. The Everett Turnpike runs north-south, and Route 101 runs east-west. The segment of the Everett Turnpike north of NH 101 and the segment of NH 101 east of the Everett Turnpike are designated Interstate 293; I-293 turns at this interchange.\nBy plane.\nManchester Boston Regional Airport ('), Route 101 exit 2, just minutes away from Bedford, it is a much more convenient option rather than going to the Logan International Airport ('). From here, you can reach all the main cities of the United States, along with Canada. The airport is not very large, and it is easy to navigate around. Has only two security checkpoints and two floors."}
